                <pb facs="0169" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg70"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/667: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-22T11:00:00-04:00">October 22, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>230. From Braden. My 228, October 19, 11 p.m. Stefanich reply poorly drafted but
                    acceptable. Finot reply satisfactory. Yesterday Conference again stressed to
                    Paraguayan delegation urgency for their prompt appointments to reglementation
                    commission, which they state will be made this week unless there is some
                    unlooked for obstacle raised in Asunción.</p>
                <p>I request authority to appoint Major Weeks to this commission. This will probably
                    entail extension of his stay in Chaco beyond November 15 when his tour as
                    military observer ends. [Braden.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
